# These files are executed inside Linux containers. core.autocrlf on a Windows
# clone would check them out with CRLF, and a shell script with CRLF endings
# fails in the container with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" -- at image build or
# first boot, long after the commit that caused it.
#
# Forced to LF regardless of the cloning machine's settings. Scoped to deploy/
# so nothing outside it is affected.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
